      "message": "did you suggest that I add this function to `ec_cmd_api.h`? If this is the case, I do not believe I can calculate the size there. The size potentially can be a large number. If you suggested that I add it inside the helper header, this is a simple change.\n\nThis is similar to [ec_cmd_battery_config](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/ec_cmd_api.h;l\u003d48?q\u003dec_cmd_api.h\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d47-,48,-49):\n\n```\nstatic inline int ec_cmd_battery_config(CROS_EC_COMMAND_INFO *h, uint8_t *r)\n{\n\treturn CROS_EC_COMMAND(h, EC_CMD_BATTERY_CONFIG, 0, NULL, 0, r,\n\t\t\t       BATT_CONF_MAX_SIZE);\n}\n```\n\nBy the way, do you have any concerns if I modify the helper function from\n\n```\nuint16_t fpinfo_cmd_helper(struct ec_response_fp_info_v2 *response)\n{\n\tstatic const size_t test_info_buffer_size \u003d\n\t\tsizeof(struct ec_response_fp_info_v2) +\n\t\tsizeof(struct fp_image_frame_params) * NUM_IMAGE_CAPTURE_TYPES;\n\n\tstruct host_cmd_handler_args args \u003d\n\t\tBUILD_HOST_COMMAND_RESPONSE(EC_CMD_FP_INFO, 2, *response);\n\targs.response_max \u003d test_info_buffer_size;\n\n\treturn host_command_process(\u0026args);\n}\n```\n\nto\n\n```\nuint16_t ec_cmd_fp_info_v2(struct ec_response_fp_info_v2 *response)\n{\n\tstatic const size_t test_info_buffer_size \u003d\n\t\tsizeof(struct ec_response_fp_info_v2) +\n\t\tsizeof(struct fp_image_frame_params) * NUM_IMAGE_CAPTURE_TYPES;\n\n\tstruct host_cmd_handler_args args \u003d\n\t\tBUILD_HOST_COMMAND_RESPONSE(EC_CMD_FP_INFO, 2, *response);\n\targs.response_max \u003d test_info_buffer_size;\n\n\treturn host_command_process(\u0026args);\n}\n```\n\nand then use it as is?",
